# Rank 1642 / CVE-2022-30123 (CWE-117): Rack::CommonLogger formats the
# request's method, path and query string into an access-log line and hands
# the result to the logger unescaped, so control characters in a request
# method such as "GET\b" forge the log output. The fixed revision escapes
# non-printable characters first:
#
#	msg.gsub!(/[^[:print:]\n]/) { |c| "\\x#{c.ord}" }
#
# Detection is a taint route with a split clearing side. The sink binding
# labels logger.write's argument code.LogOutput; the source is the
# request.query_string read. The clearing side is core.LogEscape, and the
# two String#gsub spellings need different coverage because they escape at
# different places. String#gsub returns an escaped copy, so the clean value
# is the one that leaves the call node and path coverage is exact. String#gsub!
# rewrites its receiver in place: nothing flows out of the call node, and the
# pre-mutation value keeps a direct route to the sink, so the rule's
# `unless v.dominates` clause is what clears it -- every later read inside the
# region the call dominates sees the escaped text. Splitting the bindings by
# method matters: a concrete check carries exactly one coverage mode, and two
# bindings emitting the same concept on one node compete for the label, so a
# single binding matching both spellings can only declare one of the two.
#
# The fourth case pins the boundary the split draws. A non-bang gsub whose
# result is discarded escapes nothing -- the receiver is untouched -- so it
# must not clear anything, and it does not, because only the bang spelling
# carries dominance coverage.
#
# Measured on the real checkout (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB, --cache off,
# three runs per revision, every count stable): 46 findings with 1
# VYQL-INJ-009 at the vulnerable parent (source request.query_string at
# common_logger.rb:62, sink logger.write at :72) and 45 with 0 at the fixed
# revision -- the delta is exactly the escaped write. Collateral across ten
# Ruby trees under /tmp/cve-work (vagrant, publify, publify_core,
# view_component, puma, thrift, webrick, uri, protobuf, zammad): identical
# totals and identical VYQL-INJ-009 counts both ways, including thrift's 94;
# the control-char gsub idiom occurs at exactly one site outside rack
# (webrick accesslog.rb:153, the non-bang spelling, which keeps path
# coverage) and that file reports no log finding either way.
#
# Residual, measured: dominance does not check that the escaped receiver is
# the value the sink reads. A gsub! on a different local that dominates the
# write also clears the finding. No site in the swept corpus has that shape,
# and the same looseness is shared with every other dominance-covered check
# (VYQL-CFG-014, VYQL-DESER-003).

test "rack common logger writes request-controlled text to the log unescaped"
  lang ruby
  expect VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module Rack
    class CommonLogger
      FORMAT = %{%s - %s [%s] "%s %s%s%s %s" %d %s %0.4f\n}

      def log(env, status, response_headers, began_at)
        request = Rack::Request.new(env)

        msg = sprintf(FORMAT,
          request.ip || "-",
          request.get_header("REMOTE_USER") || "-",
          request.request_method,
          request.path_info,
          request.query_string.empty? ? "" : "?#{request.query_string}",
          status.to_s[0..3])

        logger = @logger || request.get_header(RACK_ERRORS)
        if logger.respond_to?(:write)
          logger.write(msg)
        else
          logger << msg
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "the rebinding gsub spelling escapes the copy that reaches the write"
  lang ruby
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
  module Rack
    class CommonLogger
      FORMAT = %{%s - %s [%s] "%s %s%s%s %s" %d %s %0.4f\n}

      def log(env, status, response_headers, began_at)
        request = Rack::Request.new(env)

        msg = sprintf(FORMAT,
          request.ip || "-",
          request.get_header("REMOTE_USER") || "-",
          request.request_method,
          request.path_info,
          request.query_string.empty? ? "" : "?#{request.query_string}",
          status.to_s[0..3])

        msg = msg.gsub(/[^[:print:]\n]/) { |c| "\\x#{c.ord}" }

        logger = @logger || request.get_header(RACK_ERRORS)
        if logger.respond_to?(:write)
          logger.write(msg)
        else
          logger << msg
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "the fixed revision's own in-place gsub! spelling escapes the receiver"
  lang ruby
  reject VYQL-INJ-009
  code
  ```
